<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 4-week T-bills 23 pct sold, yield 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 4-week T-bills 23 pct sold, yield 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 20 billion levs of four-week floater coupon T-bills was 22.59 percent sold, yielding 16.14 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry for Monday's auction.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3021696029</p>
<p> Auction date		     December 16, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 December 18, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		    January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    4,718 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		97.72 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    4,518 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     97.99 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    16.14 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
